---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import AppCta from '../../components/AppCta.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Free stock research worksheet"
  description="Download a free stock research worksheet for Excel or Google Sheets. Record sources, business models, risks and unanswered questions."
  ><div class="container text-page">
    <h1>Your research,<br />in one place.</h1><div class="prose">
      <p>
        A watchlist tells you which companies caught your attention. A research
        worksheet records why—and what you still need to understand.
      </p><p>
        <a
          class="button button-blue"
          href="/downloads/stocker-research-worksheet.csv"
          download>Download the free worksheet ↓</a
        >
      </p><p>
        CSV format. No email required. Open it in Excel or import it into Google
        Sheets.
      </p><h2>What to record</h2><ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The business:</strong> what it sells, who pays and which competitors
          matter.
        </li><li>
          <strong>The evidence:</strong> links to filings, dates, reporting periods
          and the facts supporting your view.
        </li><li>
          <strong>The questions:</strong> what is unclear, what might go wrong and
          what would change your mind.
        </li><li>
          <strong>The follow-up:</strong> the next event or source you want to review.
        </li>
      </ul><h2>How to use it</h2><ol>
        <li>
          Download the file and open or import it as a comma-separated
          spreadsheet.
        </li><li>
          Replace the clearly labelled example row with your own company.
        </li><li>
          Keep facts and interpretations separate. Add the original source and
          date for each important claim.
        </li><li>
          Revisit the sheet after new results or a meaningful business change.
        </li>
      </ol><p>
        The worksheet does not contain live prices, formulas, brokerage
        connections or a Stocker import feature. It is a simple research
        organizer you control.
      </p><p>
        For a guided starting point, read <a
          href="/learn/how-to-research-stocks/">how to research stocks</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div><AppCta />
  </div></SiteLayout
>
